  "findings": [
    "A generated float Image with use_half_precision=False and Non-Color data exposes RGBA32F through gpu.texture.from_image.",
    "Framebuffer writes to each mip succeeded at 32 x 32 through GPUFrameBuffer(color_slots={texture: texture, mip: level}).",
    "Framebuffer writes preserve stale CPU pixels; no Image.update or Image.pixels upload was used for GPU publication.",
    "EEVEE offscreen sees GPU-only image edits after a material update tag is processed by the depsgraph. Redraw alone within one synchronous callback retains temporal history.",
    "Material-only update_tag plus view_layer.update was sufficient; a node-tree update tag was unnecessary. Production tags the material and requests redraw, leaving normal UI depsgraph processing to Blender.",
    "STRAIGHT, PREMUL and CHANNEL_PACKED Non-Color float images expose identical raw RGBA CPU and GPU samples. Float paint unpremultiplication remains an evaluator responsibility.",
    "A separate probe wrote distinct constants 0.4 through 0.9 to mip levels 0 through 5. Sampling with textureLod returned the expected value and each expected level size, proving independent mip storage and writes.",
    "The installed Metal framebuffer read_color and GLSL texelFetch paths returned mip-zero samples when testing nonzero mip levels. Mip validation therefore uses textureLod into a separate mip-zero readback texture."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Only the installed Blender 5.2.1 LTS Metal backend was measured; this is not cross-platform GPU certification.",
    "EEVEE emission viewport output used its own lower precision: 0.12345670163631439 in RGBA32F became 0.1234130859375 in the viewport.",
    "This probe does not measure compositor parity, shader/material throughput, input-to-display latency or a whole-material speed improvement.",
    "Production preserves the user-selected preview resolution; its default FULL retains authored resolution. CPU final output remains the save/export correctness path.",
    "The distinct-constant mip probe verifies storage and independent writes; general downsampling parity is covered by the live GPU math test."
  ],
